                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]First impression[/b]: Game is a 2D side-scroller that looks like a simple platformer but plays more like a NES era beat-em-up with rogue-like elements. The weapon and costume combinations are a fun twist that gives the game replayability, it was neat exploring some of the options available and getting a new piece to wear was always exciting.\n\nThe game is certainly unique so if you're a fan of rogue-likes (Risk of Rain, Binding of Isaac, etc) or clasic side-scrollers (Ghosts & Goblins, Friday the 13th, etc) then this game may be worth checking out.\n\n[b]Pros[/b]:\n[*]Procedurally generated levels make the game feel fresh (new enemies, bosses, items, etc).\n[*]Art style has a nice retro feel to it.\n[*]Costume and weapon combinations provide a bit of strategy to the game.\n[*]Reasonable price for the amount of content, seems like there's quite a few items and game modes to unlock.\n\n[b]Cons[/b]:\n[*]Game can be a bit cryptic at times. There may be a few things you weren't taught that can lead to some cheap deaths (but it might just be part of the learning curve).\n[*]Much like the classic NES era of games Haunting of Billy harkens back to there isn't much in terms of story.\n[*]Difficulty is on the higher end, like most rogue-likes. \n\n[b]Overall[/b], a fun little game from an indie developer that's worth giving a shot.\n\n\n\n[b]NOTE[/b]: I was gifted a copy of the game to review by the developer.",
